/* DISCOVERY (temporal causal pathway laws): the algebra behind chc.pathway's causal_pathway(target) --
   discover the lagged graph, estimate the dynamic effect (IRF) along each path, rank + truncate. Three
   laws, each machine-checked in proofs/causal_pathway.v:

   (L1) IRF PATH-SUM. For a stable AR(p)/SVAR the impulse response g_h (= d target_{t+h}/d shock_t) obeys
        the recursion g_h = sum_{i=1}^p a_i g_{h-i}, g_0=1, and equals the SUM OVER LAGGED WALKS of length
        h (compositions of h into parts {1..p}) of the product of edge weights -- the "which paths, of what
        sign, reach the target" decomposition (Lutkepohl, MA(inf) representation).
   (L2) GEOMETRIC HORIZON-TRUNCATION. Under a CONTRACTING operator norm ||A||=q<1 (from spectral
        radius rho<1 alone one gets only ||A^h||<=C_q q^h for q in (rho,1), Gelfand; C_q may exceed 1
        for non-normal/Jordan A), sum_{h=0}^n q^h = (1-q^{n+1})/(1-q) <= 1/(1-q) and the tail
        q^{H+1}/(1-q) decays geometrically -- so truncating at a finite horizon H loses little.
   (L3) WEAKEST-LINK / multiplicative bottleneck. A path's contribution is the PRODUCT of its edge
        magnitudes, so a path with one weak (near-zero) edge contributes negligibly: |a*b*c| = |a||b||c|,
        and |a|<=eps ==> |a*b*c| <= eps*|b||c|. The temporal-path analogue of the C2 channel bottleneck. */
display2d : false$
simpsum  : true$  /* let Maxima evaluate the symbolic geometric sum to its closed form (L2) */

/* (L1) AR(2) IRF recursion vs the walk-sum (compositions of h into parts {1,2}). */
g[0] : 1$  g[1] : a1$  g[h] := a1*g[h-1] + a2*g[h-2]$
print("L1 g2 - (a1^2+a2)             =", expand(g[2] - (a1^2 + a2)),
      "  (walks of length 2: [1,1],[2])")$
print("L1 g3 - (a1^3+2*a1*a2)        =", expand(g[3] - (a1^3 + 2*a1*a2)),
      "  (walks: [1,1,1],[1,2],[2,1])")$
print("L1 g4 - (a1^4+3*a1^2*a2+a2^2) =", expand(g[4] - (a1^4 + 3*a1^2*a2 + a2^2)),
      "  (walks: 1x[1,1,1,1], 3x length-3-with-one-2, 1x[2,2])")$

/* (L2) geometric partial-sum closed form and the decreasing tail. */
S : sum(rho^k, k, 0, n)$
print("L2 (1-rho)*sum_{0}^{n} rho^k - (1-rho^(n+1)) =", ratsimp( (1-rho)*S - (1-rho^(n+1)) ),
      "  (=> partial sum <= 1/(1-rho); Rocq: geo_sum_closed / geo_sum_bounded)")$
print("L2 tail ratio T_{H+1}/T_H - rho =", ratsimp( (rho^(H+2)/(1-rho)) / (rho^(H+1)/(1-rho)) - rho ),
      "  (=0: tail decays by factor rho<1 each step; Rocq: geometric_tail_decreasing)")$

/* (L3) weakest-link product identity. */
print("L3 abs-product: |a*b*c| = |a||b||c| (sign-free) and |a|<=eps => path <= eps*|b||c|",
      " (Rocq: weakest_link_product / weak_edge_caps_path)")$
